== Practice 7 — Editing for Capitalization (Nelson Mandela)

Corrections are in *bold*. Rules applied are noted.

1. #strong[M]y name is #strong[N]elson #strong[M]andela, and *I* have had an unusual life. [R1, R3, R2]
2. *I* have been both a prisoner and a president in my country. [R1, R2]
3. *I* was born in 1918 in a small village in #strong[S]outh #strong[A]frica. [R1, R2, R6]
4. #strong[M]y father, #strong[H]enry #strong[M]andela, was the chief of our tribe. [R1, R3]
5. #strong[A]s a child, *I* took care of the family's cattle and goats. [R1, R2]
6. #strong[W]hen *I* grew up, *I* decided to become a lawyer. [R1, R2, R2]
7. #strong[T]his seemed to be a good way to help my people. [R1]
8. #strong[A]fter *I* became a lawyer, *I* became the leader of a group of young #strong[A]fricans who wanted to change the system of discrimination in our country. [R1, R2, R2, R4]
9. #strong[B]ecause of my political activities, *I* went to prison for twenty-seven years. [R1, R2]
10. #strong[T]he prison was on a cold, windy island in the #strong[A]tlantic #strong[O]cean. [R1, R6]
11. #strong[H]owever, the world didn't forget about me. [R1]
12. *I* received important visitors, awards, and university degrees from all over the world. [R1, R2]
13. *I* also learned #strong[A]frikaans, which is the language of white #strong[S]outh #strong[A]fricans. [R1, R2, R4, R4]
14. #strong[O]f course, *I* also speak #strong[E]nglish and #strong[X]hosa, which is the language of my tribe. [R1, R2, R4, R4]
15. #strong[I]n 1990, *I* was set free. [R1, R2]
16. *I* became the president of #strong[S]outh #strong[A]frica in 1994. [R1, R2, R6]
   (Note: "president" stays lowercase — title without a name, per Rule 3 exception.)
17. #strong[D]uring my time in office, *I* tried to bring peace, democracy, and prosperity to all of my country's people. [R1, R2]
18. #strong[N]ow *I* am retired. [R1, R2]

*Rules key:*
- R1 = First word in a sentence
- R2 = Pronoun _I_
- R3 = Names of people and their titles
- R4 = Nationalities, languages, religions, and ethnic groups
- R6 = Specific places on a map

